# The project-specific redaction dictionary and the staged-byte scan patterns (release.sh steps 3 and 4).
# Anchored, because an unanchored pattern matches at any depth — the same mistake that made `lib` swallow
# `bridges/lib` in 0.6.0. This file must never reach the public repo: a copy of release.sh that travels with
# its own blocklist redacts the blocklist too, so the published script searches for the placeholder `<bot-id>`
# instead of the real value and reports a clean scan while publishing it.
/scripts/.private-blocklist
